= Class Consciousness of the New Middle Class

Due to our investments in media, socialism is becoming more popular, including among the new middle class. [? if peoples_party==0: <span style="color: #9B0000;">Marxist</span> intellectuals such as Bernstein and Kautsky have long debated about the status of the new middle class and whether they constitute a different class from the proletariat. ?][? if peoples_party==1: Despite becoming a people’s party, our party has traditionally prioritised the industrial working class. ?] Our propagandizing has meant that the new middle class are increasingly considering themselves part of the proletariat, or at least having more in common with them. Whilst they’re more moderate than the industrial proletariat, we could awaken their class consciousness as a way to expand the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span>’s base [? if peoples_party==0: without diluting its class character ?] and to build solidarity with all workers.

